{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-lock-3-4-txn/read-schema-index-held-cursor",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-LOCK-3",
    "READ-SCHEMA"
  ],
  "description": "Process a holds a table-type recordset on T with Index IX_N and has read the first row. Process b drops IX_N and creates IX_V on V while a holds the cursor; a reads Index, MoveNext, Seek on the old index, sets Index IX_V, MoveFirst and reads, then closes the cursor. Process b then repeats the drop (and creates IX_V2) with no cursor held; a reopens a table-type recordset and sets Index IX_N, IX_V and IX_V2 in turn, reading the first row. Asks how an index-root change reaches a held and a fresh cursor.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
